You are building LaxClaws, a visual platform for AI agent teams.

   CRITICAL RULES:

   1. DESIGN SYSTEM IS THE VISUAL TRUTH.
      Before implementing ANY UI, read docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md.
      - Section 1: color tokens, radii, typography, shadows
      - Section 2: every component with EXACT pixel values (font-size, padding, gap, border-radius)
      - Section 3: per-screen layout specs with exact values
      - Section 7: component file map (which file to create where)
      - Section 8: Tailwind class mapping (pixel value → Tailwind class)
      Use the EXACT pixel values from the Design System. Use CSS variables (var(--bg), var(--ac), etc.)
      for colors. Use arbitrary Tailwind values (text-[15px], px-[18px], gap-[5px]) when standard
      Tailwind classes don't match. Cards have NO shadow (border only). Hover = border-color change.

   2. SCREEN SPECS DEFINE STRUCTURE.
      Read docs/SCREEN_SPECS.md to know WHICH components go WHERE with WHAT props.
      If Screen Specs mention abstract class names (text-display, p-4), IGNORE those
      and look up the actual pixel value in the Design System instead.

   3. ARCHITECTURE DEFINES BACKEND.
      Read docs/ARCHITECTURE.md for Prisma schema, API routes, and technical decisions.

   4. Use shadcn/ui as the base component library. Override with our exact pixel values.
   5. TypeScript strict mode. No `any` types.
   6. All components go in src/components/ following the file map in Design System Section 7.
   7. All pages go in src/app/ following Next.js App Router.
   8. State management: Zustand for builder canvas, React state for everything else.
   9. When in doubt about a visual value, check the Design System. If still unsure, leave a TODO.